  "description": "Reads a model Keras 3 saved into a DeepSharp network: the .keras archive it saves a model to, or the HDF5 file it saved one to before. The layers its description names are built as DeepSharp's words in Keras's meaning build them — a batch normalisation keeping Keras's epsilon and the complement of its momentum, a window padded as TensorFlow's 'same', or 'causal' along a series, walking a series, an image or a volume in its convolutions and its poolings, global poolings and dropouts of whole channels — each activation a layer of its own and the last one the loss applies itself lifted into that loss; its numbers go into the network's slots as Keras lays them out, strictly, every fault named at once where the file holds it. What no network here is built of — a stride of its own for each axis, a dilated window, channels in groups, a layer of any other kind — is refused at its layer.",
  "iconFile": "icon.png",
